    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d722">

                <pb facs="0811" n="723" xml:id="pg723"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">835.51/897: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Argentina</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Bliss</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-04-01T15:00:00-05:00">April 1, 1933—3 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>18. Your 29, March 31, 5 p.m. Department desires to obtain your views as to
                    whether there is any possibility that the amount of British held pesos thus
                    released would exceed the amount of the loan.</p>
                <p>Last sentence, first paragraph. Why would American interests be placed at a
                    disadvantage by this loan?</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
